WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:07.259
Speaker 1: There is a new report out about
coronavirus in vaccinated people and unfortunately,

00:00:07.259 --> 00:00:14.050
as a combination of some poorly written headlines,
as well as people who may be just are not

00:00:14.050 --> 00:00:18.650
understanding the math of what's being reported,
there are people reading about this and saying,

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:21.860
oh, no, the vaccines don't work.

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:26.119
I believe that a lot of these folks are just
misunderstanding the math.

00:00:26.119 --> 00:00:33.989
Now, the new report from the CDC explains
that out of 77 million vaccinated people in

00:00:33.989 --> 00:00:42.839
the United States, it's believed that there
have been 50 800 infections, 396 people who

00:00:42.839 --> 00:00:47.839
required hospitalization and 74 people who
died.

00:00:47.839 --> 00:00:50.600
And then some of the headlines fomented.

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:57.359
What was the reaction from many individuals
who thought, oh, no, the vaccine isn't 100

00:00:57.359 --> 00:01:02.629
percent effective, which we knew no vaccine
is 100 percent effective.

00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:09.000
Another reaction was, wow, even vaccinated,
you could end up in the hospital if you get

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:10.000
the virus.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.630
And of course, we knew that as well.

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:21.700
These are incredibly powerful, efficacious
numbers of the 77 million vaccinated people.

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:30.810
Zero point zero zero zero zero nine six percent
died and this is pointing to being one of

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:38.000
the most effective vaccination programs once
we are at full strength that humanity has

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:39.720
ever seen.

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:42.430
Vaccines are not 100 percent protection.

00:01:42.430 --> 00:01:44.729
We I don't know how much more of that has
to be said.

00:01:44.729 --> 00:01:49.119
The baseline would never be this is only good
if no one ever gets sick.

00:01:49.119 --> 00:01:50.390
It's an impossible goal.

00:01:50.390 --> 00:01:55.259
It's an unreasonable goal to see this data
and to come away.

00:01:55.259 --> 00:02:01.689
Thinking the vaccine doesn't work is horrifying
because this data is really telling us how

00:02:01.689 --> 00:02:04.139
effectively the vaccines do work.

00:02:04.139 --> 00:02:08.670
And then to get this gets to a lot of black
and white thinking.

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:14.120
That has been a problem during the pandemic
unmasks remember, do the masks work or don't

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:15.120
they?

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:16.120
Either they do or they don't.

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:17.220
They either work perfectly or they don't work
at all.

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:18.390
Well, no, it's a percentage.

00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:22.680
If one person has a mask, you're reducing
in a physical sense with a physical barrier,

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:23.680
the spread of the virus.

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:27.340
If two people have a mask, well, then you're
reducing it even further.

00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:29.989
The vaccine, it's not one hundred percent.

00:02:29.989 --> 00:02:35.650
We understand that if one person in an interaction
is vaccinated, the possibility of spread goes

00:02:35.650 --> 00:02:40.099
down because the vaccinated person is 90 percent
less likely to spread and ninety two to ninety

00:02:40.099 --> 00:02:42.510
five percent less likely to get it.

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:47.790
So if they they're less likely to give it
to the unvaccinated person, they're less likely

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:49.790
to get it from the unvaccinated person.

00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:54.019
If you have two people interacting who are
vaccinated, the possibility of the spread

00:02:54.019 --> 00:02:55.480
is even smaller.

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:59.379
And if someone were to get it out of the vaccinated
people, it would be less serious.

00:02:59.379 --> 00:03:02.409
And if it were serious, you would be less
likely to die.

00:03:02.409 --> 00:03:04.290
That's these are confidence intervals.

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:05.920
That's how everything works.

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:09.379
This really is some of the best news that
we could have hoped for.

00:03:09.379 --> 00:03:13.980
And it's important to know there's actually
this these numbers may improve over time.

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:21.090
On the one hand, it's true that of those 77
million vaccinated people over time, as more

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:26.019
of those individuals are out in the world
and are potentially exposed, some more of

00:03:26.019 --> 00:03:27.530
them are going to get the virus.

00:03:27.530 --> 00:03:28.560
That's true.

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:35.760
But as more people get vaccinated, the interactions
that that cohort of 77 million has is going

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:41.160
to increasingly be with vaccinated people,
and that's going to reduce the contagion even

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:42.160
further.

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:44.129
So we're dealing with a lot of different things
right now.

00:03:44.129 --> 00:03:47.930
We've got the pause on the Johnson and Johnson
vaccine.

00:03:47.930 --> 00:03:51.870
Countries and the U.S. are still figuring
out to some degree supply and distribution.

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:56.640
We are waiting to see because cases have just
been trickling up, although deaths have been

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:59.290
continuing down, as we said yesterday or the
day before.

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:04.080
We're waiting to see when will we really see
the drop in cases that Israel saw.

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:08.300
Israel saw it somewhere between 50 and 55
percent vaccinated.

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:11.390
We're probably a month from that in the United
States.

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:15.959
Some states are closer, sadly, because of
vaccine hesitancy.

00:04:15.959 --> 00:04:17.910
Some states are further away.

00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:25.540
But the important take away is how insanely
effective these vaccines are.

00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:30.920
The CDC data confirms that and restates that.

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:32.750
And that should really be the focus.

